469 0 obj
<<
/A 1939 0 R
/Alt (Illustration comparing multilayer and multiplex network architectures for multi-omics data integration. Panel a shows stacked data layers \(genomics, epigenomics, transcriptomics, proteomics, metagenomics, exposomics, clinical data\) connected by solid and dashed lines, leading to tasks such as diagnosis, biomarker identification, prognosis, therapies personalization, and monitoring. Panel b contrasts multilayer and multiplex networks using diagrams and equations, highlighting intra-layer and inter-layer edges and the relationships among nodes and layers.)
/K [24 1940 0 R]
/P 141 0 R
/Pg 51 0 R
/S /Figure
/T (FIGURE 2)
/Type /StructElem
